{{!< default}}

{{!-- The sign-in Surface.

Ghost renders the members flow through Portal, which a theme cannot template — but Portal is a
modal a reader opens, and a publication that wants a sign-in ADDRESS to send people to needs a
page. This is that page, and it reimplements nothing: `data-members-form` and `data-members-email`
are Ghost's own contract, Portal binds the submit out of {{ghost_head}}, and the report comes back
as classes on the form.

The residual gap — that every entry point in the Chrome opens Portal's own drawing rather than
this one — is recorded as a Concession in DECISIONS.md.

The state matrix lives in auth/shell.hbs, which both auth Surfaces share. --}}

{{> "chrome/header" auth=true}}

{{> "auth/shell"
	flow="signin"
	surface="sign-in"
	eyebrow=(t "Members")
	title=(t "Sign in")
	subhead=(t "Members read the interviews, the transcripts and the archive.")}}
